			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement Cocoon initialization handshake and operation cancellation\n\nIntroduce three new gRPC handlers in the `Mountain` backend to formalize the startup sequence and lifecycle management with the Cocoon extension host sidecar:\n\n- `InitialHandshake`: A ping from Cocoon to signal readiness, acknowledging the connection before data transfer.\n- `InitExtensionHost`: Receives workspace folder lists and configuration from the client, parsing and persisting them into `ApplicationState.Workspace` via `WorkspaceFolderStateDTO` to ensure the boot path has access to the current workspace context.\n- `CancelOperation`: Enables cancellation of in-flight operations by looking up the request identifier in `Service.ActiveOperations` and firing the associated token.\n\nThese handlers adhere to the project's PascalCase naming conventions (`Fn`, `DTO`) and explicit trait method resolution patterns. This completes the foundational IPC contract required for the extension host to receive state and support graceful operation termination.",
			"SHA": "b0a8fa23c5d8797b0a011977b8f1c59073f3c700"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:31:54Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1003,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Apply explicit trait resolution for gRPC extension notifications\n\nCorrect the invocation of `Vine::Client::SendRequest` in `NotifyCocoonDeltaExtensions` by switching from direct call syntax to explicit trait method resolution (`::Fn`). The previous syntax failed to resolve the trait method in the current compilation context, preventing the dispatch of `$deltaExtensions` and `$activateByEvent` notifications to the Cocoon extension host.\n\nThis aligns the IPC handler with the strict trait-based interaction patterns established in recent fixes for `PickFolder` and other Wind service handlers, ensuring reliable gRPC communication between the Mountain backend and the Cocoon sidecar.",
			"SHA": "41e2292edc78f7ded8fcee80584bcc758db0ed0d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:31:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1003,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Canonicalize path resolution in ConfigurationProvider\n\nUpdate the import structure in `ConfigurationProvider/Loading.rs` and `ConfigurationProvider/UpdateValue.rs` to use the explicit nested path resolution for `ApplicationRunTime`. Replace the deprecated `RuntimeStruct::ApplicationRunTime` with the flattened canonical path `ApplicationRunTime::ApplicationRunTime`, aligning with the recent module flattening strategy applied to `ExtensionState` and `ConfigurationState`.\n\nAdditionally, correct the type signature in `collect_default_configurations` to reference the fully qualified canonical path `ApplicationState::State::ApplicationState::ApplicationState`. This ensures consistent symbol resolution across the `Mountain` backend and adheres to the project's strict PascalCase naming conventions for module hierarchies.",
			"SHA": "429aa1f742bb34e1554c3f3d4416c7f196ade0ad"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:31:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1003,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Canonicalize path resolution in PickFolder handler\n\nUpdate the import structure in `Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers/NativeHost/PickFolder.rs` to use explicit nested path resolution for `ApplicationState` and `UpdateWorkspaceFoldersAndBroadcast`. Replace the wildcard-style direct imports with the fully qualified path under `State::`.\n\nThis change aligns `PickFolder` with the recent module flattening strategy applied to `ConfigurationState`, `ExtensionState`, and `Keybindings`, ensuring consistent symbol resolution and adherence to the project's strict PascalCase naming conventions for module hierarchies.",
			"SHA": "fd18b0640561c1048b8f272dd0ec346cdac4bd43"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:31:34Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1003,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Correct method invocation on Client::SendNotification\n\nChange the invocation of `Client::SendNotification` from direct function call syntax to explicit trait method resolution (`::Fn`). The previous syntax failed to resolve correctly in the current compilation context, causing a build error when dispatching workspace folder deltas to the Cocoon extension host.\n\nThis ensures the notification `$deltaWorkspaceFolders` is successfully sent to the \"cocoon-main\" client upon workspace changes, adhering to the strict trait-based interaction patterns used in the Mountain backend.",
			"SHA": "5ae45559141de37b2e1ee90ac139df85a2e3412c"
		}
	],
